# Smart App Control On (by-hand.md's Bootstrap, plan row 46): the snapshot bootstrap-sac.suite runs
# from. From a snapshot with SAC in Evaluation ("clean Windows"), kept running, then taken by the
# host (no owner step):
#   tests/win/vm-run.sh run "clean Windows" sac --keep
#   tests/win/vm-run.sh snapshot "SAC On"
# sac-on sets VerifiedAndReputablePolicyState to 1, refreshes the Code Integrity policies and
# restarts Windows; Windows signs the user in by itself (no autologon of ours is set: a snapshot
# never carries one); sac-check reads the state back (the registry, Defender) and sees our
# unsigned hidden.exe blocked. The steps are ConstrainedLanguage-safe (sac/lib.ps1, not vmlib),
# in case SAC On runs our scripts in ConstrainedLanguage. Without --keep the run reverts the VM as
# any other. Not a release.list row.
include sac/lib.ps1
# MODE       SECS NAME          SCRIPT
sys          300  sac-on        sac/on.ps1
wait         600  sac-restart   logon
sys          120  sac-check     sac/check.ps1
